The standard deviation of the sampling distribution of the mean (i.e., the standard error under the null hypothesis) is

\[
\sigma_{\bar{x}}=\frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
=\frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
\approx \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
\approx 0.22.
\]

So the standard deviation of the null‑hypothesis test is about **0.22**.
